WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.000
A sound has a shape. You can draw it, measure it, replay it.

00:00:07.000 --> 00:00:14.000
A claim about what that sound does inside a person needs a different kind of evidence.

00:00:14.000 --> 00:00:21.000
Here is the mistake: because the arrows on a diagram connect, we think the science is connected too.

00:00:21.000 --> 00:00:28.000
In two thousand and two, researchers described how familiarity can masquerade as explanation.

00:00:28.000 --> 00:00:35.000
Try a free twelve-minute audit. Write down every missing step.

00:00:35.000 --> 00:00:42.000
An audio library can offer structure; its promises still need proof. Final Vestige investigates the difference.
